I am excited to apply for the Teacher and Digital Competency Leader role. Having taught both Computer Science and Mathematics for nine years, I have seen first-hand how impactful high quality digital skills provision can be. Over the past three years, my passion for breaking down barriers between students and technology has only deepened, and I am eager to take on a role that allows me to inspire both students and teachers on a much wider scale.

I have mentored teachers who are new to teaching both Mathematics and Computer Science and collaborated across departments to redesign Electrical and Electronic Engineering modules to meet shifting specifications. Key to this was listening to the needs of colleagues and respond with practical, supportive solutions. I aim to foster a collaborative environment and support the professional growth of others in any setting I find myself in.

I have had the opportunity to teach many subjects with a strong mathematical basis. I have also sought out additional opportunities to use my skills to create, evaluate and improve various resources for students to work on. This ranges from research-driven PRIMM worksheets to procedural question generation for Dr Frost Maths. Building on a deep passion for the use of computing in the wider world, I have been able to use my pedagogical expertise and subject knowledge develop high-quality resources for teachers and students alike.

I am enthusiastic about engaging students beyond the classroom, allowing them to see their skills solve problems, engage with industry partners, and build the soft skills vital to their futures. I have led student engineering teams to a variety of national competitions and am currently collaborating with colleagues to develop an outreach program aimed at addressing gender disparities within STEM. By actively working to widen participation and ensuring that all learners see success throughout the curriculum, I hope to take every chance to help St Martin's remove barriers to success for students from all backgrounds.

Having balanced nine years of teaching with a variety of other roles, I have developed both the technical rigor and pedagogical insight necessary to thrive in this position. This foundation, combined with my teacher mentorship and a drive to help students engage with technology in a meaningful way, ensures I am well-prepared to contribute to St Martin's mission of enhancing digital educational standards and accessibility. I am eager to bring this same level of enthusiasm to the St Martin's team and welcome the opportunity to discuss my application further. Please do not hesitate to reach out should you have any questions or require additional details regarding my background.

Sincerely,\ 
Timothy Grace